# ✅ Notice:
# The “Testing utils module...” part didn’t appear — because it’s inside the if __name__ == "__main__": block in utils.py.

# 💡 Why this is useful :

# It lets you:

# => Write functions and classes in one file.
# => Test them freely in the same file.
# => Import them anywhere else without the test code running again.
